guide("/septic-for-home-inspectors/","Septic Pump-Outs and Inspections for Home Inspectors in SWFL | Express Septic",
 "A partner page for home inspectors in Southwest Florida: how to request a $549.99 septic inspection with pump-out, what we will and will not report, and how to reach Express at (239) 451-3261.",
 "Septic pump-outs and inspections for home inspectors",
 "<p><strong>Home inspectors walking a Southwest Florida property on a septic tank often need a specialist who can actually open and pump the tank, not another generalist.</strong> This page is for inspectors who want a clear way to point clients toward that visit. We are not home inspectors, and this is not a substitute for your own report. A septic inspection with pump-out is $549.99. Call <a href='tel:"+TEL+"'>"+PHONE+"</a>, or have the buyer or seller <a href='"+BOOK+"' rel='noopener' target='_blank'>request a routine time on ServiceM8</a>. We confirm the appointment with the person who can provide access.</p>"
 "<h2>What can you ask Express to do during the inspection period?</h2>"
 "<p>We can pump the tank and, on the inspection visit, tell the parties what we saw. That is the same $549.99 inspection with pump-out described on our <a href='/septic-inspections/'>septic inspections</a> page and in the <a href='/buying-or-selling-a-home-with-septic/'>buying or selling</a> guide. A pump-out alone, when someone only needs the tank emptied and already knows the system, starts at $399.99 for a standard 1–3 bedroom home. We do not perform the general home inspection, test every fixture in the house, or complete an appraisal. If you have already noted odors, lush spots, or slow drains, say so when the visit is scheduled so we arrive with that context.</p>"
 "<h2>What will we report, and what will we not claim?</h2>"
 "<p>We tell you what we observed at the tank: access, whether we pumped both compartments, whether a filter was present and cleaned (we clean it at no charge on pump-outs), and anything we saw that needs attention. We do not invent a remaining life for a drain field, issue a 'certification' that a lender is required to accept, or sign off on work we have not been asked to inspect in depth. Drain field replacement or repairs, if they come up, are quoted after we inspect the system. That limit is honest, and it keeps your client from thinking a pump-out is a warranty.</p>"
 "<h2>How should an inspector hand off the scheduling?</h2>"
 "<p>Send the client to us with the property address, the inspection deadline, and who holds the keys or gate code. Realtors have a short briefing at the <a href='/septic-guide-for-realtors/'>Realtor septic guide</a>; you do not need to become the go-between for every phone tag, but it helps if one person owns the appointment. If nobody can find the lid, <a href='/cant-find-septic-tank-lid/'>locating and digging</a> is $100, plus $50 for each additional hour. Older homes with no paperwork are covered on <a href='/older-homes-septic-systems/'>older homes with septic systems</a>.</p>"
 "<h2>What if the client is using an FHA or VA loan?</h2>"
 "<p>Lenders, appraisers, and underwriters decide what documentation a particular loan needs. We do not decide eligibility. Official FHA and VA starting points are summarized, with citations, on <a href='/fha-va-lender-septic-requirements/'>FHA, VA, and lender septic requirements</a>. If a party asks us for an inspection with pump-out to help answer a condition, we can do that visit. Whether it satisfies the condition is not something we can promise in advance.</p>"
 "<h2>What should you note in the yard before we arrive?</h2>"
 "<p>Wet or extra-green areas over a possible drain field, a sewage odor, an alarm panel, obvious buried lids, and whether the house is occupied all help. You already know how to write those observations into your own report. If sewage is actively backing up, the client should call us as an emergency, not wait for a routine slot; after-hours pumping is $599.99. We serve inspectors and their clients in Lee, Collier, and Charlotte County, plus LaBelle.</p>"
 "<p><a class='btn primary' href='tel:"+TEL+"'>Call "+PHONE+"</a> <a class='btn ghost' href='"+BOOK+"' rel='noopener' target='_blank'>Book routine service on ServiceM8<span class='sr'> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p>",
 HI_FAQ, "Home inspectors")

