 "<h2>What if the kitchen is on Bonita Springs Utilities?</h2>"
 "<p>The "+BSU_POL+" requires grease interceptors to be completely evacuated at least every 90 days, or sooner if 25% or more of the wetted height contains floating materials, sediment, or FOG. Complete removal of grease, water, and solids is required, and pump-and-return is prohibited. BSU's maintenance card also asks facilities to send manifests or receipts to BSU within 30 days. That is the kitchen's paperwork duty. This page does not claim that Express provides manifests, is a licensed grease hauler, or handles compliance reporting. More Bonita-specific detail is on <a href='/grease-trap-pumping-bonita-springs-fl/'>grease trap pumping in Bonita Springs</a>.</p>"
