 "<p>Business 41 (the older Tamiami corridor) and Hancock Bridge Parkway hold much of the area's food service, with more kitchens along Pine Island Road toward Cape Coral. The riverfront and the bridges into downtown Fort Myers bring commuter and visitor traffic that still spikes in winter, even if this side of the river is less of a tourist strip than Fort Myers Beach. We do not name private restaurants as customers. City-of-Fort-Myers addresses should use <a href='/grease-trap-pumping-fort-myers-fl/'>grease trap pumping in Fort Myers</a>; Cape Coral addresses should use <a href='/grease-trap-pumping-cape-coral-fl/'>Cape Coral</a>.</p>"
