 "Restaurant grease trap and interceptor pumping service areas in Southwest Florida, including Lee, Collier, and Charlotte County city pages. $695 for a 1,000-gallon unit. Call (239) 451-3261.",
 "Grease trap and interceptor pumping service areas",
 "<p><strong>Express Septic pumps restaurant grease traps and interceptors across Southwest Florida.</strong> Start with a city page below for local corridors and the FOG rules we could verify for that utility. The service-area price for a 1,000-gallon grease trap or interceptor is $695, and other sizes are quoted when you call. Call <a href='tel:"+TEL+"'>"+PHONE+"</a> or <a href='"+BOOK+"' rel='noopener' target='_blank'>open a routine booking on ServiceM8</a>. The service overview is <a href='/grease-trap-pumping/'>grease trap and interceptor pumping</a>.</p>"
 "<h2>Lee County area cities</h2>"
 "<ul class='cards'>"
 "<li><a href='/grease-trap-pumping-bonita-springs-fl/'><strong>Bonita Springs</strong></a> — Old 41, Bonita Beach Road, and BSU's 90-day interceptor rule (and 25% wetted-height trigger) for BSU sewer customers.</li>"
