 "<li><a href='/grease-trap-pumping-fort-myers-beach-fl/'><strong>Fort Myers Beach</strong></a> — Estero Boulevard and Times Square. Confirm the sewer provider; Lee County Utilities customers follow Ordinance 14-24.</li>"
 "<li><a href='/grease-trap-pumping-cape-coral-fl/'><strong>Cape Coral</strong></a> — Cape Coral Parkway, Del Prado, and Pine Island Road. Cape Coral Utilities sets the schedule for city sewer customers; confirm current requirements.</li>"
 "<li><a href='/grease-trap-pumping-lehigh-acres-fl/'><strong>Lehigh Acres</strong></a> — Lee Boulevard and inland commercial streets. Typical Lee County Utilities accounts follow Ordinance 14-24.</li>"
 "<li><a href='/grease-trap-pumping-north-fort-myers-fl/'><strong>North Fort Myers</strong></a> — Business 41 and Hancock Bridge Parkway. Unincorporated Lee County; typical LCU accounts follow Ordinance 14-24.</li>"
 "<li><a href='/grease-trap-pumping-san-carlos-park-fl/'><strong>San Carlos Park</strong></a> — U.S. 41 between Fort Myers and Estero. Typical LCU accounts follow Ordinance 14-24; some sites are still on septic.</li>"
 "<li><a href='/grease-trap-pumping-sanibel-fl/'><strong>Sanibel</strong></a> — Periwinkle Way and the Causeway. Confirm the current City of Sanibel Utilities grease schedule.</li>"
