filter_city("/septic-filter-cleaning-estero-fl/","Septic Filter Cleaning in Estero, FL | Effluent Filter Care | Express Septic",
 "Effluent filter cleaning for Estero homes still on septic. Filter cleaned at no charge during pump-out; we can show you how to keep it clear. Risers $299.99 each. Call (239) 451-3261.",
 "Septic filter cleaning in Estero, FL",
 "<p><strong>Express is based in Estero, and many Village homes are still on a septic tank even as sewer work moves in phases.</strong> If that tank has an effluent filter, keeping it clear is one of the simplest ways to avoid a backup that shows up without warning. We are at 23357 Olde Meadowbrook Circle. We clean the filter at no charge during a pump-out and can show you the outlet side so you know what you are looking at later. Call <a href='tel:"+TEL+"'>"+PHONE+"</a> or <a href='"+BOOK+"' rel='noopener' target='_blank'>send an Estero routine request on ServiceM8</a>.</p>"
 "<h2>Does filter care still matter while the Village converts streets to sewer?</h2>"
 "<p>Yes. The Village of Estero is converting properties to Lee County Utilities sewer in phases, a program described in more detail on our <a href='/septic-tank-pumping-estero-fl/'>Estero septic pumping</a> page and aimed in part at protecting the Estero River. Early work has included package-plant communities and Broadway Avenue areas, and the Village treats connection as mandatory once sewer reaches a property. Until your street is connected and the tank is abandoned, wastewater still goes through the tank and, if you have one, through the effluent filter. A conversion notice is not a reason to ignore a slow drain this week.</p>"
 "<h2>Where is the filter, and what happens when it clogs?</h2>"
 "<p>It is in the outlet of the tank, under the lid farthest from the house inlet. When the screen loads up with solids, the tank cannot send wastewater out as designed. Drains in the kitchen or bath slow, gurgle, or back up, sometimes overnight after a heavy use day. People often assume the tank itself is overdue. Sometimes it is. Sometimes the filter is the bottleneck. We check both when we pump. There is no single numbered cleaning interval on this page, because household size and use in Estero vary; the rule we use is to clean it at every pump-out and whenever drains start to slow.</p>"
 "<h2>Access in Village yards and HOA lots</h2>"
 "<p>Some Estero lids sit in open lawns. Others are under ornamental planting or in a side yard that is easy to miss if you bought the house recently. If we have to find and dig a buried lid, the charge is $100, plus $50 for each extra hour. A <a href='/septic-tank-riser-installation/'>6-inch riser</a> at $299.99 each brings that opening to grade, which is useful in a mowed yard where you want to check the filter without opening a hole in the turf each time. Ask us to install it while the tank is already open for pumping.</p>"
 "<h2>How a dirty filter relates to the drain field</h2>"
 "<p>The filter's job is to keep solids in the tank. If it is missing, damaged, or so clogged that wastewater finds another path, solids can move toward the drain field. Healthy soil bacteria can treat liquid effluent; they cannot undo a field that has been overloaded with sludge. We are not quoting a failure rate for Estero fields. We are saying that a cheap, regular filter cleaning is a poor thing to skip if you want the field to keep working until, or unless, sewer arrives. More general background is on <a href='/septic-filter-care/'>septic filter care</a> and <a href='/septic-bacteria-drain-field/'>good bacteria and the drain field</a>. If a backup is already in progress after hours, pumping is $599.99; call rather than using the form. Other cities are listed on the <a href='/septic-filter-cleaning-service-areas/'>filter service-areas hub</a>.</p>"
 "<p><a class='btn primary' href='tel:"+TEL+"'>Call "+PHONE+"</a> <a class='btn ghost' href='"+BOOK+"' rel='noopener' target='_blank'>Book an Estero filter visit on ServiceM8<span class='sr'> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p>",
 ESF_FAQ, "Estero filter cleaning")
