 "<h2>Why the well and the filter belong in the same conversation</h2>"
 "<p>On a well-and-septic lot, the drain field and the well are in the same soil. Pumping on schedule keeps sludge in the tank. The filter is the last screen on the way out. If it is packed, wastewater can back up into the house. If it is missing or damaged, solids can move toward the field. We will not invent a well-contamination statistic. We will say that a clean filter is one of the few inexpensive steps that protects both the house plumbing and the field on a lot like this.</p>"
