 "<h2>What a dirty filter does when the yard is already wet</h2>"
 "<p>Low yards and river-side streets can stay wet in the rainy season. That does not mean every slow drain is a flooded field, and it does not mean the filter can be ignored. A packed filter can send wastewater back into the house on its own. A field that is already dealing with a high water table has less room if solids get past a neglected screen. We will not invent a flood-zone statistic or a depth to water. We will clean the filter at the pump-out, and we will clean it if you call because drains have already slowed. That is the interval we publish. If a backup is already in progress after hours, pumping is $599.99; call rather than using the form.</p>"
