 "<h2>Pavers in the town center, grass on the edge of town</h2>"
 "<p>In the compact center, a lid can sit under pavers. On a parcel outside the core, it may be out in the yard, farther from the driveway. In either case the filter is under the outlet lid. Uncovering a buried lid is $100, plus $50 for each extra hour. Bringing that lid to grade with a 6-inch riser costs $299.99 each, which is often the difference between a short later check and another excavation. Tell us which situation you have when you book.</p>"
 "<h2>What a packed filter does during a busy week</h2>"
 "<p>If the screen clogs, wastewater can back toward tubs and sinks even if the tank still has room. A missing or damaged screen can let solids travel toward the drain field. Cleaning it will not rebuild a field that has already failed, and it will not replace pumping. It will remove a bottleneck that often gets blamed on a 'full tank' when the outlet was the actual obstruction.</p>"
 "<h2>The Estates next door are a different system story</h2>"
