 "<p><strong>Pine Island is the largest island in Lee County, and many homes and businesses here still use a septic tank, so filter care is a routine part of owning the lot, not a rare leftover.</strong> The island is not one kind of yard. Bokeelia, Pineland, St. James City, and Matlacha sit on the same island and can have very different access, canal frontage, and how close the water table feels after a rain. This page is for those households whose outlet filter needs to stay clear so a backup does not show up without warning. When a filter is there, we clean it during the pump-out and can walk you through seating it again. Call <a href='tel:"+TEL+"'>"+PHONE+"</a> or <a href='"+BOOK+"' rel='noopener' target='_blank'>request a Pine Island visit on ServiceM8</a>.</p>"
