 "<h2>Canal-front wet yards and what a packed screen can cause</h2>"
 "<p>When the outlet clogs, wastewater can turn back toward fixtures even if the tank is not completely full. On a low canal lot, a wet yard after rain can make that backup feel even more urgent, but the wet yard is not a substitute for a clear filter. Solids can travel toward the drain field when the screen is missing or damaged. Cleaning the filter will not replace a field that has already failed. It will take away a bottleneck that is often blamed on the tank being 'due' when the outlet was the obstruction.</p>"
 "<h2>Getting to the island is part of the plan</h2>"
 "<p>Pine Island is reached from the mainland on Pine Island Road, through Matlacha, and a mid-morning weekday is often easier than a late Friday. That is only scheduling. The work does not change: we empty the tank, clean an outlet filter if one is there, and can walk you through the seating. Finding and uncovering a lid that is no longer visible is billed at $100, then $50 an hour after that. The published 6-inch riser price is $299.99 each, and that brings that lid to grade so a later check on a canal-side or inland lot does not start with a dig.</p>"
 "<h2>No numbered interval, even though many lots have tanks</h2>"
 "<p>Because so many Pine Island properties still use septic, it can be tempting to look for a single island-wide filter calendar. We will not publish one. Clean the filter when we empty the tank, and check it if drains start to slow before the next pump-out. Seasonal use in any of the four communities can change the load; it does not create a required month.</p>"
 "<h2>This is not the Sanibel or Fort Myers Beach page</h2>"
 "<p>Sanibel is a Gulf-side city with a refuge and a different sewer-and-tank mix. Fort Myers Beach is a low, sandy gulf island along Estero Boulevard. Pine Island is a larger, more residential and fishing-community island with four named towns and many tanks still in use. Use the page that matches the house. The overview of filter care, not the local access notes, is on <a href='/septic-filter-care/'>septic filter care</a>. Tank pumping, as opposed to this filter page, is on <a href='/septic-tank-pumping-pine-island-fl/'>septic tank pumping on Pine Island</a>. Other communities are listed on the <a href='/septic-filter-cleaning-service-areas/'>filter service-areas hub</a>. A standard 1 to 3 bedroom tank starts at $399.99 for residential pumping. After-hours work while a backup is already happening is $599.99; call.</p>"
